Defect: with the PGO profile of a clang and lld training build (LLVM_PROFDATA_FILE), clang 23.1.4 at -O3 compiles flang/lib/Evaluate/expression.cpp for more than three hours (29 seconds without the profile). The profile holds no samples of flang code, so flang gains nothing from it.
Upstream status: not reported upstream; local packaging policy of a PGO build whose training covers clang and lld only.
Version-bump check: build the final stage and confirm that every flang source compiles in minutes; drop this patch when flang/lib/Evaluate compiles quickly with -fprofile-instr-use.

--- a/flang/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/flang/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -497,6 +497,12 @@
   add_compile_definitions(FLANG_INCLUDE_TESTS=1)
 endif()
 
+# The PGO profile of the build holds no samples of flang, and clang spends hours
+# on some template-heavy flang sources with it.
+if (LLVM_PROFDATA_FILE)
+  add_compile_options(-fno-profile-instr-use)
+endif()
+
 add_subdirectory(include)
 add_subdirectory(lib)
 add_subdirectory(cmake/modules)
